1
00:00:03,640 --> 00:00:09,270
Wall Maria contained one third
of humanity's remaining territory.

2
00:00:10,360 --> 00:00:13,860
Five years ago,
when humanity lost this territory,

3
00:00:14,240 --> 00:00:17,470
from within the remaining
two walls, they realized:

4
00:00:18,330 --> 00:00:22,370
"That we...
are not meant to continue living."

5
00:00:23,710 --> 00:00:28,010
After all,
humanity cannot defeat the Titans.

6
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:30,500
I'm going to drive out...

7
00:00:30,880 --> 00:00:34,970
...every last one from this world!

8
00:00:36,180 --> 00:00:40,940
However, one young man gripped
that small blade held in his heart,

9
00:00:41,640 --> 00:00:46,750
and thrust it into a Titan, pounding its
massive head into the ground.

10
00:00:47,980 --> 00:00:52,150
When humanity saw this,
what did they think?

11
00:00:53,530 --> 00:00:55,320
Some were proud.

12
00:00:56,030 --> 00:00:57,870
Some held hope.

13
00:00:58,700 --> 00:01:01,200
Some cried out in anger.

14
00:01:02,790 --> 00:01:08,960
Then, if Wall Maria was retaken,
what would humanity cry out?

15
00:01:10,040 --> 00:01:15,050
Would they finally start believing
that humanity deserves to live?

16
00:01:15,310 --> 00:01:18,970
Advance!

17
00:01:21,890 --> 00:01:25,270
That our own fate is
something we can decide?

18
00:01:26,020 --> 00:01:28,800
Will it be enough for them to believe?

19
00:01:30,520 --> 00:01:34,370
If only Wall Maria was retaken...

20
00:03:09,960 --> 00:03:14,960
"The Town Where Everything Began"

21
00:03:21,510 --> 00:03:22,510
Whoa!

22
00:03:22,511 --> 00:03:25,219
Hey! You've gotta light up the ground!

23
00:03:25,220 --> 00:03:26,660
S-Sorry.

24
00:03:27,010 --> 00:03:30,269
We're not at the foot yet?
It's almost dawn.

25
00:03:30,270 --> 00:03:33,900
Once we're over this mountain,
Shiganshina's right there.

26
00:03:35,520 --> 00:03:37,780
Sorry you're stuck with my horse.

27
00:03:38,190 --> 00:03:40,739
You're supposed to be saving your energy.

28
00:03:40,740 --> 00:03:42,279
Yeah, I know.

29
00:03:42,280 --> 00:03:44,739
She's right. Rest up, Eren.

30
00:03:44,740 --> 00:03:46,409
Don't say his name, idiot.

31
00:03:46,410 --> 00:03:48,699
Oh, yeah, sorry.

32
00:03:48,700 --> 00:03:51,690
Assume this place is
swarming with enemies.

33
00:03:53,920 --> 00:03:57,290
Titan on the left! Everyone halt!
Light up the area!

34
00:04:00,130 --> 00:04:02,599
It's all right. He's fast asleep.

35
00:04:02,600 --> 00:04:06,170
This lad must not be one of those
new types that moves at night.

36
00:04:07,430 --> 00:04:10,470
That's too bad. Let him be.

37
00:04:16,610 --> 00:04:19,939
I can't believe we didn't
see it till that close up.

38
00:04:19,940 --> 00:04:22,609
Yeah, I'm with you there.

39
00:04:22,610 --> 00:04:26,659
This moonless night must be protecting us.

40
00:04:26,660 --> 00:04:29,700
Light from the moon is reflected sunlight.

41
00:04:30,260 --> 00:04:31,619
The new type of Titan...

42
00:04:31,620 --> 00:04:36,430
We think they use that minuscule
amount of reflected light to move.

43
00:04:36,880 --> 00:04:39,380
Using the new moon was the right move.

44
00:04:40,170 --> 00:04:43,630
There's no guarantee we won't
have a repeat of before.

45
00:04:44,380 --> 00:04:48,420
That lad may be one of those
"Moonlight Titans" for all we know.

46
00:04:49,430 --> 00:04:52,270
Hope we capture one someday!

47
00:04:59,980 --> 00:05:01,250
I'm shaking?

48
00:05:02,570 --> 00:05:05,750
Why? What am I so scared of?

49
00:05:07,240 --> 00:05:08,240
Shit...

50
00:05:08,870 --> 00:05:12,450
If I screw up retaking Wall Maria
because I'm like this, what then?!

51
00:05:13,500 --> 00:05:15,880
How many people will lose hope forever?

52
00:05:16,370 --> 00:05:19,290
There won't be a chance
like this ever again!

53
00:05:20,750 --> 00:05:23,020
Am I not cut out for it after all?

54
00:05:23,710 --> 00:05:28,139
Someone like me? How can I save humanity?

55
00:05:28,140 --> 00:05:30,640
Someone like me? How?

56
00:05:33,100 --> 00:05:34,389
Eren...

57
00:05:34,390 --> 00:05:38,599
What are you shaking for? Are you scared?

58
00:05:38,600 --> 00:05:40,859
Huh?! I'm not scared!

59
00:05:40,860 --> 00:05:44,280
Huh? You're kidding... Look at your hand.

60
00:05:44,440 --> 00:05:49,279
This is... It's cold!
My hand's damn freezing!

61
00:05:49,280 --> 00:05:53,650
Really? My whole body's been
shaking this whole time.

62
00:05:54,660 --> 00:05:55,600
See?

63
00:05:59,330 --> 00:06:02,220
Eren, have you ever been afraid of Titans?

64
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:06,800
Normally, everyone's terrified of them.

65
00:06:07,130 --> 00:06:13,090
Like me... The first time I faced a Titan,
I couldn't move a muscle.

66
00:06:13,850 --> 00:06:16,420
But... there I was...

67
00:06:16,770 --> 00:06:19,390
And you pulled me right
out of a Titan's mouth.

68
00:06:20,600 --> 00:06:23,760
How were you able to
do something like that?

69
00:06:27,990 --> 00:06:29,260
I remembered...

70
00:06:29,990 --> 00:06:32,530
...the time you showed me that book.

71
00:06:33,990 --> 00:06:37,910
Up until then, I never once thought
about what was outside the walls.

72
00:06:39,330 --> 00:06:42,740
I just spent every day
staring at the clouds and sky.

73
00:06:44,630 --> 00:06:49,060
But then, I heard your story
and looked into your eyes.

74
00:06:51,090 --> 00:06:53,440
You were seeing an awesome dream.

75
00:06:54,090 --> 00:06:55,470
But I had nothing.

76
00:06:56,770 --> 00:06:58,730
That's when I knew.

77
00:06:59,440 --> 00:07:01,150
I wasn't free.

78
00:07:02,560 --> 00:07:04,526
Trapped in a small
cage in a huge world,

79
00:07:04,551 --> 00:07:07,924
my freedom stolen by
those unthinkable fiends.

80
00:07:09,190 --> 00:07:12,960
When I realized that,
I couldn't forgive them.

81
00:07:14,120 --> 00:07:18,800
I don't know why, but when it
comes to taking back freedom...

82
00:07:19,660 --> 00:07:23,220
Yes... Strength flows through me.

83
00:07:26,270 --> 00:07:27,460
Thanks for that.

84
00:07:27,960 --> 00:07:29,259
I'm good now.

85
00:07:29,260 --> 00:07:30,919
Mmm.

86
00:07:30,920 --> 00:07:36,260
I bet, by this time next year,
we'll be looking at the sea.

87
00:07:40,480 --> 00:07:42,940
I recognize this area.

88
00:07:45,150 --> 00:07:49,030
I think... we came here for firewood.

89
00:07:52,070 --> 00:07:54,699
I can see the foot!

90
00:07:54,700 --> 00:07:56,620
There's signs of a trail!

91
00:07:58,910 --> 00:08:01,249
It's so close.

92
00:08:01,250 --> 00:08:03,289
I can hear the river.

93
00:08:03,290 --> 00:08:06,590
Finally, we're back...

94
00:08:08,210 --> 00:08:11,760
The first time... since we fled from here.

95
00:08:13,050 --> 00:08:15,430
Back to our hometown...

96
00:08:32,360 --> 00:08:35,949
Be on guard for Titans
hiding in the shadows!

97
00:08:35,950 --> 00:08:38,329
Our operation begins now!

98
00:08:38,330 --> 00:08:41,660
All troops, switch to ODM gear!

99
00:08:49,920 --> 00:08:54,339
There's two gates we must seal...
the inner and outer.

100
00:08:54,340 --> 00:08:56,639
With that, Shiganshina will be isolated.

101
00:08:56,640 --> 00:08:59,180
We'll exterminate any Titans left inside.

102
00:09:00,140 --> 00:09:04,180
If the enemy knows our plan,
they'll go straight after Eren, but...

103
00:09:08,980 --> 00:09:14,489
We'll have hoods covering the faces
of all 100 of our soldiers.

104
00:09:14,490 --> 00:09:19,410
By the time they find out who Eren is,
we'll have the outer gate plugged.

105
00:09:32,920 --> 00:09:34,919
Don't stop!

106
00:09:34,920 --> 00:09:37,379
Head for the outer gate!

107
00:09:37,380 --> 00:09:38,510
Roger!

108
00:09:43,390 --> 00:09:45,139
This is...

109
00:09:45,140 --> 00:09:47,060
...the remains of a fire?

110
00:09:50,860 --> 00:09:54,149
They're here... and close!

111
00:09:54,150 --> 00:09:56,110
Bertholdt and Reiner!

112
00:10:03,540 --> 00:10:06,289
My house is right around there.

113
00:10:06,290 --> 00:10:10,250
That's where... we left everything behind.

114
00:10:17,590 --> 00:10:20,550
It's okay, I'll take it all back!

115
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:27,229
This is all too strange...

116
00:10:27,230 --> 00:10:30,189
Not a single Titan in sight?

117
00:10:30,190 --> 00:10:32,019
But we have to keep going.

118
00:10:32,020 --> 00:10:35,610
Yeah, there's no reason to call it off.

119
00:10:42,070 --> 00:10:45,869
I can do this! No...

120
00:10:45,870 --> 00:10:48,659
We can do this!

121
00:10:48,660 --> 00:10:54,289
Because we've all been special
since the day we were born!

122
00:10:54,290 --> 00:10:56,510
We're free!

123
00:11:47,640 --> 00:11:49,929
Don't let your guard down!

124
00:11:49,930 --> 00:11:51,269
Keep on the lookout!

125
00:11:51,270 --> 00:11:52,480
Roger!

126
00:11:54,770 --> 00:11:55,730
Eren!

127
00:11:55,731 --> 00:11:57,979
How's your ODM gear?

128
00:11:57,980 --> 00:11:59,489
It's fine.

129
00:11:59,490 --> 00:12:02,610
But I did manage to lose my cloak.

130
00:12:07,740 --> 00:12:09,159
Thanks.

131
00:12:09,160 --> 00:12:10,869
Mmm.

132
00:12:10,870 --> 00:12:13,039
The hole?!

133
00:12:13,040 --> 00:12:14,500
Success!

134
00:12:15,540 --> 00:12:17,540
It's plugged all right!

135
00:12:21,130 --> 00:12:23,219
We did it!

136
00:12:23,220 --> 00:12:24,639
Eren, you okay?

137
00:12:24,640 --> 00:12:26,139
No problems here.

138
00:12:26,140 --> 00:12:27,929
I'm ready like we trained.

139
00:12:27,930 --> 00:12:29,769
We'll head for the inner gate!

140
00:12:29,770 --> 00:12:33,390
While we're on the move,
remember to hide your faces!

141
00:12:36,270 --> 00:12:40,399
I really plugged the hole?
And that easily...?

142
00:12:40,400 --> 00:12:42,029
You did it.

143
00:12:42,030 --> 00:12:44,110
Believe in your own power.

144
00:12:46,950 --> 00:12:48,990
The hole from then...

145
00:12:51,750 --> 00:12:53,369
Not yet!

146
00:12:53,370 --> 00:12:58,129
No matter how much you plug it, they'll
break the wall as long as they live.

147
00:12:58,130 --> 00:13:01,759
Until we kill Reiner, Bertholdt,
and any other enemies,

148
00:13:01,760 --> 00:13:04,679
the operation to retake
Wall Maria won't end.

149
00:13:04,680 --> 00:13:07,260
Of course... I know that!

150
00:13:09,260 --> 00:13:12,139
The outer gate was a success.

151
00:13:12,140 --> 00:13:14,639
Still, it's odd...

152
00:13:14,640 --> 00:13:16,809
There's no attack coming.

153
00:13:16,810 --> 00:13:21,859
On the contrary, we've not seen
a single Titan so far.

154
00:13:21,860 --> 00:13:25,449
Were they not prepared
for our sudden assault?

155
00:13:25,450 --> 00:13:27,279
We can only hope, but...

156
00:13:27,280 --> 00:13:29,829
Considering what Arlelt discovered...

157
00:13:29,830 --> 00:13:31,699
Hmm?

158
00:13:31,700 --> 00:13:33,289
I looked into it.

159
00:13:33,290 --> 00:13:36,709
I'm pretty sure someone was camping.

160
00:13:36,710 --> 00:13:40,879
The pot was cold and lights
were scattered on the ground.

161
00:13:40,880 --> 00:13:43,710
They were drinking
something like black tea.

162
00:13:45,260 --> 00:13:49,009
Smells good... What is this drink?

163
00:13:49,010 --> 00:13:53,469
Also, there were three cups
with drops of a black liquid in it.

164
00:13:53,470 --> 00:13:56,519
At the least, there were
three people atop the wall.

165
00:13:56,520 --> 00:13:58,849
Th-Three, you say?!

166
00:13:58,850 --> 00:14:01,269
Was the metal pot completely cool?

167
00:14:01,270 --> 00:14:02,190
Yes.

168
00:14:02,191 --> 00:14:03,529
I find that odd.

169
00:14:03,530 --> 00:14:04,440
Agreed.

170
00:14:04,441 --> 00:14:07,239
Th-The pot?

171
00:14:07,240 --> 00:14:12,789
We charged here at full speed
using horses and ODM gear.

172
00:14:12,790 --> 00:14:17,119
Had they noticed our approach
by sound or by sight,

173
00:14:17,120 --> 00:14:19,789
they'd have two minutes to react.

174
00:14:19,790 --> 00:14:24,049
A pot in use wouldn't
cool in just two minutes.

175
00:14:24,050 --> 00:14:28,339
They had to have known we were
coming for five minutes or more.

176
00:14:28,340 --> 00:14:31,969
Meaning they've had plenty
of time to prepare for us.

177
00:14:31,970 --> 00:14:34,179
But... how?

178
00:14:34,180 --> 00:14:39,019
Th-There must be a scout in addition
to the three on the wall...

179
00:14:39,020 --> 00:14:43,899
No, we have to assume there's
many more enemies in hiding.

180
00:14:43,900 --> 00:14:47,109
For now, locating the
enemy is our priority.

181
00:14:47,110 --> 00:14:48,399
Arlelt...

182
00:14:48,400 --> 00:14:52,949
With that brain of yours, you've saved
us from disaster countless times.

183
00:14:52,950 --> 00:14:56,249
Right now is one of
those times we need you.

184
00:14:56,250 --> 00:14:58,119
Huh?

185
00:14:58,120 --> 00:15:00,209
Take as many soldiers as needed.

186
00:15:00,210 --> 00:15:03,500
Find out if enemies are hiding
near the inner gate or not.

187
00:15:05,800 --> 00:15:09,299
As of now,
you obey Armin Arlelt's commands.

188
00:15:09,300 --> 00:15:11,300
Continue the search!

189
00:15:15,890 --> 00:15:16,720
R...

190
00:15:16,721 --> 00:15:17,889
Roger!

191
00:15:17,890 --> 00:15:19,979
We searched the wall thoroughly!

192
00:15:19,980 --> 00:15:22,270
What are your orders, Arlelt?!

193
00:15:24,230 --> 00:15:26,569
Send one group to each side of the wall!

194
00:15:26,570 --> 00:15:29,189
Search all the buildings
near the inner gate!

195
00:15:29,190 --> 00:15:31,910
Report any findings
with an acoustic shell!

196
00:15:33,240 --> 00:15:36,489
A-All right?

197
00:15:36,490 --> 00:15:37,750
Roger!

198
00:15:41,830 --> 00:15:43,629
Another big gamble of yours?

199
00:15:43,630 --> 00:15:46,669
No, he's proven himself.

200
00:15:46,670 --> 00:15:49,919
He's one of our greatest weapons.

201
00:15:49,920 --> 00:15:52,629
Eren's coming to plug the inner gate.

202
00:15:52,630 --> 00:15:54,049
What now?

203
00:15:54,050 --> 00:15:57,010
Pause the operation
until we find the enemy?

204
00:15:58,810 --> 00:16:00,979
We continue.

205
00:16:00,980 --> 00:16:04,359
We'll lose a prolonged battle
in enemy territory.

206
00:16:04,360 --> 00:16:08,729
For us, our only chance
is with a decisive battle.

207
00:16:08,730 --> 00:16:14,989
Besides, if this is all according to the
enemy's plan, we'll just have to live with it.

208
00:16:14,990 --> 00:16:19,790
In any case, they're not the
only ones hiding something.

209
00:16:26,340 --> 00:16:28,589
What do I do?

210
00:16:28,590 --> 00:16:32,009
Eren's coming to seal the inner gate...

211
00:16:32,010 --> 00:16:34,680
And we don't know where the enemy's at!

212
00:16:35,760 --> 00:16:39,809
Why haven't they shown
even though we plugged the wall?

213
00:16:39,810 --> 00:16:43,639
Why can't we find them
no matter how much we search?

214
00:16:43,640 --> 00:16:46,059
This is bad... What now?

215
00:16:46,060 --> 00:16:49,729
If we fail... that'll really be the end!

216
00:16:49,730 --> 00:16:52,609
It's over. Everything...

217
00:16:52,610 --> 00:16:57,199
They always attack us in unthinkable
ways we always fail to predict.

218
00:16:57,200 --> 00:16:59,579
We're always at a disadvantage because...

219
00:16:59,580 --> 00:17:02,870
...we simply know nothing about Titans!

220
00:17:03,910 --> 00:17:05,500
Always...?

221
00:17:21,810 --> 00:17:23,429
Did you find them, Arlelt?!

222
00:17:23,430 --> 00:17:24,390
Where are they?!

223
00:17:24,391 --> 00:17:27,349
Not yet! Everyone search the walls!

224
00:17:27,350 --> 00:17:29,269
I told you we already did!

225
00:17:29,270 --> 00:17:30,899
There's nowhere to hide!

226
00:17:30,900 --> 00:17:32,650
Inside the walls!

227
00:17:33,820 --> 00:17:35,149
Inside the walls?

228
00:17:35,150 --> 00:17:36,319
Yes!

229
00:17:36,320 --> 00:17:40,409
There must be a spot where someone
could stay inside for a long time!

230
00:17:40,410 --> 00:17:42,330
How do you know that?!

231
00:17:45,160 --> 00:17:46,290
It's a hunch.

232
00:17:47,170 --> 00:17:50,589
Do you have any idea what
sort of situation we're in?!

233
00:17:50,590 --> 00:17:53,009
We don't have time to waste on hunches!

234
00:17:53,010 --> 00:17:54,669
Think about it!

235
00:17:54,670 --> 00:17:59,349
The enemy always attacks us using
Titan powers in ways we never imagine!

236
00:17:59,350 --> 00:18:02,429
If we constrain ourselves to
common sense and reason,

237
00:18:02,430 --> 00:18:05,430
we'll never be able to
gain the upper hand!

238
00:18:13,900 --> 00:18:16,149
The signal to halt the mission!

239
00:18:16,150 --> 00:18:19,029
All troops,
scatter and stand by atop the wall!

240
00:18:19,030 --> 00:18:20,490
Roger!

241
00:18:22,120 --> 00:18:25,749
There are times to be strict
and times to be flexible.

242
00:18:25,750 --> 00:18:29,999
Adhere to the principles you vowed
while giving everything you've got.

243
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:32,209
Obey the chain of command.

244
00:18:32,210 --> 00:18:35,260
The reason we are here
is to claim victory!

245
00:18:37,800 --> 00:18:40,679
Break into two groups again
and search the surface!

246
00:18:40,680 --> 00:18:42,639
Especially above the gate!

247
00:18:42,640 --> 00:18:44,470
Commence the search!

248
00:18:45,520 --> 00:18:46,390
Rog...

249
00:18:46,391 --> 00:18:47,770
Roger!

250
00:18:55,230 --> 00:18:57,149
What are they doing?

251
00:18:57,150 --> 00:19:00,109
Should we really be waiting like this?

252
00:19:00,110 --> 00:19:03,950
Yeah, so much for our surprise attack...

253
00:19:04,910 --> 00:19:08,370
Armin... Did you figure something out?

254
00:19:16,420 --> 00:19:21,049
A position to react, no matter
when Eren appears...

255
00:19:21,050 --> 00:19:24,099
A position able to see everything...

256
00:19:24,100 --> 00:19:28,389
If there is such a place,
it has to be in the walls.

257
00:19:28,390 --> 00:19:32,769
If the enemy has no idea we know
about the Titans in the walls,

258
00:19:32,770 --> 00:19:36,069
and they think we'll
never see it coming...

259
00:19:36,070 --> 00:19:37,400
Or possibly...?

260
00:19:44,160 --> 00:19:47,040
Here! There's a cavity here!

261
00:19:59,050 --> 00:20:00,380
Reiner!

262
00:20:18,440 --> 00:20:19,400
Shit!

263
00:20:19,400 --> 00:20:20,030
...Captain?!

264
00:20:20,030 --> 00:20:20,690
...Is that another Titan power?!
...Captain?!

265
00:20:20,691 --> 00:20:21,859
...Is that another Titan power?!

266
00:20:21,860 --> 00:20:25,370
So close! But I couldn't finish 'em!

267
00:20:43,130 --> 00:20:45,339
Keep on the lookout!

268
00:20:45,340 --> 00:20:47,260
Locate his allies!

269
00:21:23,050 --> 00:21:24,799
Boulder incoming!

270
00:21:24,800 --> 00:21:26,760
Get down!

271
00:21:31,180 --> 00:21:32,389
What the...?!

272
00:21:32,390 --> 00:21:34,019
Did he miss?

273
00:21:34,020 --> 00:21:37,899
No... That was good aim.

274
00:21:37,900 --> 00:21:43,069
He plugged the entrance.
Now the horses can't pass.

275
00:21:43,070 --> 00:21:45,489
They'll aim for the
horses and surround us...

276
00:21:45,490 --> 00:21:50,079
...in order to block our escape
and annihilate us here.

277
00:21:50,080 --> 00:21:52,949
We're both hoping for the same thing.

278
00:21:52,950 --> 00:21:56,039
To settle it here once and for all.

279
00:21:56,040 --> 00:21:58,209
Humanity or Titans?!

280
00:21:58,210 --> 00:22:02,420
Which side will live?!
Which side will perish?!

281
00:23:41,020 --> 00:23:44,649
A horde of Titans appears out of nowhere.

282
00:23:44,650 --> 00:23:46,939
As they vie to settle the fight,

283
00:23:46,940 --> 00:23:53,369
the once friend becomes enemy
and stands in Eren's way.

284
00:23:53,370 --> 00:23:54,619
Next episode: "Thunder Spears."

285
00:23:54,620 --> 00:23:56,589
"Thunder Spears"
